# Every failing disjunct reports its own error, also when the disjuncts
# share their positions, as the enum members the JSON Schema decoder
# produces do.
# https://cuelang.org/issue/4477

! exec cue vet data.json jsonschema: schema.json
cmp stderr expect

-- schema.json --
{"$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema", "enum": [1, 2, "three"]}
-- data.json --
0
-- expect --
3 errors in empty disjunction:
conflicting values 0 and "three" (mismatched types int and string):
    ./data.json:1:1
    ./schema.json:1:76
invalid value 0 (out of bound ==1):
    ./schema.json:1:70
    ./data.json:1:1
invalid value 0 (out of bound ==2):
    ./schema.json:1:73
    ./data.json:1:1
